{#
  view/juser/login/login.phtml — ask for a sign-in link.

  This page was two pages until 2026-08-20: /user/login and /user/register, differing only
  in wording, because under the old password model registering and signing in were genuinely
  different acts. Under magic links they are the same request — an unknown address simply
  becomes an account — so the second route was retired and the copy has to serve both
  readers at once. That is why it says "If you don't have an account yet, this creates one"
  rather than having a second page say so.

  `form_hidden` on `redirect`, not `form_row`: the .phtml calls `formHidden()`, which emits
  the input with no label, no wrapper and no error block. A `form_row` here would render an
  empty Bootstrap form-group around a hidden input — visible as vertical space on a page
  whose whole content is one field.

  **No `action` attribute**, hence `form_open(form, '')`: the .phtml never calls
  `setAttribute('action', …)`, so laminas emits none and the browser posts to the current
  URL — which is what carries `?redirect=` through a submission that fails validation.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Sign in') }}</h1>

<p>{{ translate("Enter your email address and we'll send you a link to sign in. There's no password to choose or remember. If you don't have an account yet, this creates one.") }}</p>

{{ form_open(form, '') }}
{{ form_row(form.get('email')) }}
{{ form_hidden(form.get('redirect')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}

<p class="help-block">{{ translate('The link works once and expires shortly after we send it.') }}</p>
{% endblock %}
